      "message": "nit: This could be simplified by using an atomic enum with three states (Unknown / True / False) instead. Given that the result of the computation is the same from any thread, this could even avoid any locking when trying to compute this concurrently. Wdyt?\n\nAlso, name could be `does_export_public_inputs` for consistency with the `has_` prefix for other flags.\n\nE.g.\n\n```\n// A boolean flag evaluated on demand.\nenum class LazyBool {\n  Unknown,\n  True,\n  False,\n};\n\nstd::atomic\u003cLazyBool\u003e does_export_public_inputs \u003d ExportsPublicInputsValue::Unknown;\n...\n\nbool ExportsPublicInputs(const Target* target) {\n  TargetInfo* info \u003d GetTargetInfo(target);\n  LazyBool value \u003d info-\u003edoes_export_public_inputs.load(std::memory_order_acquire);\n  if (value \u003d\u003d LazyBool::Unknown) {\n    // optional locking can be added here.\n    value \u003d ComputeExportsPublicInputs(info);\n    info-\u003edoes_export_public_inputs.store(value ? LazyBool::kTrue : LazyBool::kFalse, std::memory_order_release);\n  }\n  return (value \u003d\u003d LazyBool::True);\n}\n...\nbool ComputeExportsPublicInputs(info) {\n  if (!target-\u003epublic_inputs().empty())\n    return true;\n  for (const auto\u0026 dep : target-\u003epublic_deps()) {\n    if (ExportsPublicInputs(dep.ptr))\n      return true;\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n```",
